EQUATION fun_KS.cpp
MODELREPORT modelreport.html

DESCRIPTION

Object_Root

END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_init
Model initialization (all countries) (run only once)
END_DESCRIPTION

Variable_runCountry
Execute the time steps for all countries
END_DESCRIPTION

Object_Country
Country object
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagAddWorkers
Additional (migrant) workers on full employment
0 = vegetative worker population growth (as per parameter delta)
1 = additional growth (delta+1%) during full employment (Ue<1%) periods
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagAllFirmsChg
Capital-good sector firm-specific regime change
0 = only a fraction of new firms at t=TregChg change
1 = all firms change at t=TregChg
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagCons
Consumption composition
0 = C = Q2 + N (ignore unfilled past demand)
1 = C = Q2 + N + Cpast (unfilled past consumption recovered at once)
2 = C = Q2 + N + min( Cpast, Crec ) (recover past consumption with limit Crec)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagCreditRule
Bank total credit supply rule
0 = no bank-level credit limit (firm-level prudential limit still apply)
1 = Basel-like bank capital adequacy rule
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagExitCredit
Exit equity credits handling
0 = use exit credits to pay for entry equity costs and save the rest (cExitAcc)
1 = return (net) exit credits to consumers
2 = return period net exit credits to government (reduce public debt)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagExpect
Firm expectation in consumption-good sector
0 = myopic expectations with 1-period memory
1 = myopic expectations with up to 4-period memory
2 = accelerating GD expectations
3 = 1st order adaptive expectations
4 = extrapolative-accelerating expectations
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder1
Firing order in capital-good sector
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 4.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder1Chg
Firing order in capital-good sector after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 5.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder2
Firing order in consumption-good sector
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 4.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireOrder2Chg
Firing order in consumption-good sector after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 5.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireRule
Consumption-good sector firing rule operation
0 = never fires (always except for retirement) ("Japanese mode")
1 = never fires with sharing ("German mode")
2 = only fire if firm downsizing ("French mode")
3 = only fire if firm is at losses ("Italian mode")
4 = fire if payback is achieved ("American mode")
5 = always fire when contract ends ("Brazilian mode")
6 = regime 5 until t=T and then regime Y ("increasing protection")
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFireRuleChg
Consumption-good sector firing rule operation after regime change
_INIT_
All 3 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagFiscalRule
Government fiscal rule
0 = no fiscal rule (fixed unemployment benefit rate)
1 = balanced budget rule with maximum deficit on GDP
2 = soft balanced budget rule with maximum deficit on GDP (only if GDP growing)
3 = balanced budget rule with maximum debt and deficit on GDP
4 = soft balanced budget rule with maximum debt and deficit on GDP (only if GDP growing)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagGovExp
Government expenditure
0 = no public expenditure (except net interest and bail-outs)
1 = growing fixed government expenditure
2 = pay unemployment benefit
3 = pay unemployment benefit and spend government superavit if no public debt
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHeterWage
Wage indexation heterogeneity
0 = firm and worker level homogeneous (economy productivity indexes wages)
1 = firm-level heterogeneity only (firms productivity index wages)
2 = worker-level heterogeneity (positive workers productivity index wages)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder1
Hiring order in capital-good sector
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder1Chg
Hiring order in capital-good sector after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 6.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder2
Hiring order in consumption-good sector
0 = random order
1 = higher wage workers first
2 = lower wage workers first
3 = higher skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
4 = lower skills workers first (requires flagWorkerLBU=1 to be meaningful)
5 = higher payback period workers first
6 = lower payback period workers first
7 = old hired workers first
8 = recent hired workers first
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireOrder2Chg
Hiring order in consumption-good sector after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 6.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireSeq
Consumption-good sector hiring sequence
0 = firms hire workers in random order
1 = firms offering higher wages  first
2 = firms without workers hire first then random order
3 = firms without workers hire first then higher wages order
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagHireSeqChg
Consumption-good sector hiring sequence after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagIndexMinWage
Minimum wage indexation
0 = no minimum wage adjustment
1 = periodic minimum wage adjustment (value in ]0,1] to weight indexation)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagIndexMinWageChg
Minimum wage indexation after regime change
_INIT_
All 3 instances equal to 0.99.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagIndexWage
Wage indexation
0 = no wage adustment during employment
1 = periodic wage adjustment (according to flagHeterWages)
2 = current wage offer replication to existing workers (consumption-good sector only)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagIndexWageChg
Wage indexation after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagLearn1
Worker-level learning in capital-good sector
0 = no learning, preserve skills
1 = no learning, reducing skills (like unemployed)
2 = learning, increasing skills (like consumption-good sector)
3 = learning with minimum skills
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagMachDeliv
Labor shortage effect on machine production
0 = labor shortage does not affect new machines delivery
1 = labor shortage affects machine delivery proportionally
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagSearchDisc
Job search discouragement
0 = always search
1 = global search probability (aggregate unemployment)
2 = individual search probability (individual unemployment)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagSearchMode
Job search mode
0 = always search
1 = search only if unemployed
2 = search if unemployed or wage is below average
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagSearchModeChg
Job search mode after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagTax
Taxation
0 = taxes on firm profit only
1 = taxes on firm profit and worker income (wage/bonus
)
2 = taxes on firm profits and worker and capitalist income
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagWageOffer
Wage offer mode
0 = propose wage premium (don't consider requested wages)
1 = propose lowest possible wage based on workers' requested wages
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagWageOfferChg
Wage offer mode after regime change
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagWagePremium
Wage premium mode
0 = no premium (keep current wage)
1 = indexation mechanism (WP1)
2 = endogenous mechanism (WP2)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagWorkerLBU
Worker-level learning cumulativeness
0 = no worker-level learning
1 = worker-level learning-by-using-vintage
2 = worker-level learning-by-tenure
3 = worker-level learning-by-using-vintage & learning-by-tenure
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_flagWorkerSkProd
Worker skills effect on productivity in consumption-good sector
0 = no effect of worker skills on productivity (firm-level skills not affected)
1 = only worker vintage skills affect productivity
2 = only worker tenure skills affect productivity
3 = both worker vintage & tenure skills affect productivity
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_Crec
Unfilled past consumption recover limit
(as fraction of current consumption)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_FcBasMax
Maximum number of basic consumption-good industries
(1 <= FcBasMin <= Fc0bas <= FcBasMax)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 10.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_FcBasMin
Minimum number of basic consumption-good industries
(1 <= FcBasMin <= Fc0bas <= FcBasMax)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 3.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_FcLuxMax
Maximum number of luxury consumption-good industries
(0 <= FcLuxMin <= Fc0lux <= FcLuxMax)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 10.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_FcLuxMin
Minimum number of luxury consumption-good industries
(0 <= FcLuxMin <= Fc0lux <= FcLuxMax)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_Fc0bas
Initial number of industries in basic-goods subsector
(>0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 5.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_Fc0lux
Initial number of industries in luxury-goods subsector
(>0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_TregChg
Regime change period (new policies introduction)
If set to zero, there is no regime change
(>=0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 200.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_alpha3
First Beta distribution parameter for complexity drawing
(>0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 2.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_beta3
Second Beta distribution parameter for complexity drawing
(>0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 4.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_chiC
Replicator dynamics selectivity coefficient
 between consumption-good industries
(>0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 0.25.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_delta1
Competitiveness weight for price
(>=0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_delta2
Competitiveness weight for quality
(>=0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_delta3
Competitiveness weight for newness
(>=0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
END_DESCRIPTION

Parameter_delta4
Competitiveness weight for complexity
(>=0)
_INIT_
All 1 instances equal to 1.
